;
; Bring up every network interface configured under DEVS:NetInterfaces/. Each
; file there describes one interface (see the examples in SYS:Storage/NetInterfaces).
; The installer does NOT wire this into S:User-Startup -- deliberately, because
; some hardware (WiFi especially) is not ready that early and a bring-up that
; fails at boot is harder to diagnose than one you ran yourself. Run it by hand,
; or add "Execute S:Network-Startup" to your User-Startup once your setup works.
;
; The pattern ~(#?.info) matches every file EXCEPT Workbench .info icons.
FailAt 30
AddNetInterface DEVS:NetInterfaces/~(#?.info)

; Set the clock from the network. Many Amigas have no working battery clock and
; boot with a meaningless date, which quietly breaks file timestamps and anything
; comparing them. Failure here must never hold up the network, so it is run
; detached and its output goes to a log rather than the boot screen.
;
; Comment this out if you keep time some other way, or change the server -- a
; local router usually answers NTP and is faster than pool.ntp.org.
Run >NIL: C:sntp pool.ntp.org >RAM:sntp.log
